WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.500
Speaker 1: . I have a voicemail here from
someone who is not pleased with my position

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:06.850
on outdoor masks.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:12.179
Now, I think it's really important for me
to state again, my position is that I think

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:14.690
I am going to listen to the CDC unmasks.

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:17.040
My position has been that all along.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:21.550
And this person, like many in the audience,
are sort of upset with me about me saying

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:25.770
I think the CDC is right about pulling back
on outdoor masking in most situations.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.090
Let's take a listen to this and go piece by
piece.

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:33.359
Speaker 7: Hey, David, you say you not for
wearing masks because again,

00:00:33.359 --> 00:00:38.539
Speaker 1: I've been wearing a mask outdoors
this entire time, I didn't think it was necessary,

00:00:38.539 --> 00:00:41.579
but I've been doing it because I just follow
the CDC guidelines.

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:43.329
The CDC guidelines have now changed.

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:45.329
It's not that I am for or against.

00:00:45.329 --> 00:00:46.660
I am listening to the CDC.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:51.989
Speaker 7: My question for you is, would you
be OK with someone smoking at the same table

00:00:51.989 --> 00:00:56.569
as you outdoors or smoking right next to the
door of your office building?

00:00:56.569 --> 00:00:58.390
Speaker 1: So I guess two things.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.909
They're smoking at the same table.

00:01:00.909 --> 00:01:02.460
I don't really know any smoker.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:05.830
So there's no reason somebody should be smoking
at my table.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:09.650
If you mean the next table over, there's a
bunch of differences here.

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:15.260
Covid particles are water droplets or aerosolized
liquid.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.220
If you want to go in that direction, cigaret.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.440
Smoke is smoke.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.720
So the physics of it is totally different.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.790
Covid particles aren't carcinogenic.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.920
They don't have a cumulative effect over your
lifetime.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:31.500
Secondhand smoke is something that it has
a cumulative effect on the body over lifetime.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.860
There is some amount of covid particles that
could make you sick.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:39.160
And if it's below that threshold, then that's
it.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:41.840
Accumulating cigaret smoke over a lifetime
is bad.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.640
So the analogy is the same one Tucker Carlson
made, but it's not a good one.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:49.400
Speaker 7: Or smoking right next to the open
window of your apartment.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.430
I'm guessing you would complain about that.

00:01:52.430 --> 00:02:00.570
And I'm asking what evidence you have that
carcinogens in cigarets are able to move as

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:01.590
far.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:04.350
Or they are able to move further than covid
virus.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:10.530
Speaker 1: Yeah, listen, I these are two completely
different things.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.780
Smoke is smoke.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:14.450
Covid particles are are liquid.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:17.140
So it's just none of it is making sense to
me.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:25.590
We also know that it's not like the covid
and cigarets are also dissimilar in that essentially

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:27.120
no one's getting sick outside.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.680
Before anybody was vaccinated, the estimate
is one out of a thousand cases were transmitted

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:32.700
outdoors.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.400
And we have to believe that those few outdoor
cases were people doing obviously stupid things,

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:41.920
a big crowd on a hiking trail or at a concert
or whatever the case may be.

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:42.920
There's just no analogy.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.680
We know it's not an issue.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.220
People have not been getting sick in that
way.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.830
Speaker 7: Particles.

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:54.060
And I'm also wondering if you're not for wearing
masks outdoors.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:59.980
If someone goes from outdoors to indoors,
they put their mask in their pocket.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:05.190
What's preventing the particles on one side
of the mask from infecting the other side

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.190
of the mask?

00:03:06.190 --> 00:03:11.500
Well, it's in the pocket and the particles
collected on the mask from getting onto the

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.880
hands of people.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:13.880
Oh, God, how are you?

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.220
How do you expect people to manage this?

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:16.500
I don't think most people can.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.330
Speaker 1: It's what's been the I mean, the
entire time, you know, you go in somewhere,

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:23.220
you put your mask on, then at some point the
mask goes in your pocket.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.010
This is basically surface transmission.

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:28.460
Surface transmission has been shown to be
almost zero.

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:33.190
Remember, at the beginning, all this stuff
about bleach, your vegetables and all of this

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.470
different stuff, it's been determined it's
not necessary.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:37.470
Mask in the pocket.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:40.250
Then on the face, the particles move around.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:41.620
That's not how people are getting sick.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.170
So I'm not worried about that.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.730
There's no evidence that I need to worry about
that better.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:50.970
Speaker 7: That it was just in and out of
your pocket, you've just moved everything

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.500
the mask has collected into your pocket.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.270
Speaker 1: Anyway, yeah, right.

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:59.530
But again, we now know that that type of surface-to-surface
stuff is not how people are getting sick.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:05.290
So my question to these folks is, if you agreed
with the CDC all along, why do you suddenly

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:08.230
now not believe what the CDC is saying?

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:11.390
I've just been listening to the CDC from the
start.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:15.879
I think that that voicemail is completely
antithetical to any known science.

